# bend-cad: completeness, for solve_complete (DESIGN §10.4 "C6 plan",
# C6d), over the system solved (PLAN-sk13a S5, S7). Proofs only.
# Generated: python3 tools/expand.py tools/drafts/completepf.draft lib/completepf.bend
#
# At the level l whose first precision is P = P_l: the solver's plan at P
# is the blocks in turn (lib/pblkpf.bend's pb_ok) over the system solved
# (the pass's positions, matched and pinned by dependence, blocks by what
# its equations mention: lib/skdpf.bend) from the pins' box (the pins at
# the drawing's values, radius 0, which is x there); the whole verdict
# passes (the plan checker, the side conditions of the constraints neither
# red nor amber, the pins held, and the exact checks, which hold whatever
# the drawing: lib/ckpf.bend); so the precision loop stops at P and the
# answer holds x. A >= 0 side over pins only is checked at its exact
# value (the pins' balls have radius 0); the others with room. Only the
# system solved needs dyadic constants, and the sketch less its red
# constraints gives them (lib/vrdpf.bend: dy_solved).

